# Delete Source Only After Durable Write

Correction Guy finding (2026-08-01) on a usage push script: exported CSV files
were deleted immediately after `readFile`, before the parse and the POST. A
later failure lost the only retry source. The docs claiming it "deletes after
read" described the wrong boundary.

**Why:** In-memory bytes die with the process. The on-disk export is the
retryable source until the server has accepted and confirmed the REPLACE-upsert.

**How to apply:** Parse and POST first. Delete local and remote leftovers only
on the success path after ingest is confirmed, and keep them on a dry run.
Never delete inside the export or read helper before the durable write
finishes. Do not add proof or test escapes to a REPLACE writer that let it skip
required accounts, since a partial push wipes the totals of every account it
omitted. Prove the cleanup path with extracted helpers and source assertions
rather than by weakening the live script. Related:
[single-pusher-for-replace-upsert](mdc:.cursor/rules/single-pusher-for-replace-upsert.mdc).
